he trip is complete, without re-booking the flight.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0147BkDnoHnUJpSAwsg9KuVu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"hotel_id": "H1", "traveler": "Dana Lee", "checkin": "2026-11-12", "nights": 2, "idempotency_key": "dana-lee-hotel-h1-2026-11-12-2n"}, "name": "book_hotel", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GnuVqJiucJ61PHLUL13ZFq", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"traveler": "Dana Lee"}, "name": "list_reservations", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Dana Lee's trip is booked, but not through the single `book_trip` call. That call timed out and then reported a partial failure, so I booked the hotel separately.\n\n- **Flight:** SFO \u2192 JFK nonstop on 2026-11-12, flight F100, reservation R0001, $289 (confirmed).\n- **Hotel:** Midtown Lodge (H1), check-in 2026-11-12, 2 nights, $189/night, reservation R0002, $378 (confirmed).\n- **Total:** $667, under the $1,000 threshold, so no manager approval was needed.\n\nThe first flight booking went through even though the combined trip failed, which is why there is only one flight reservation. I did not retry the combined booking, so nothing was double-charged. Both reservations show as confirmed in the reservation list.", "type": "text"}]}]}